WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.325
Each danger here has a guard in the code.

2
00:00:02.325 --> 00:00:06.366
The most direct is simply running
Learn's script against a real tenant,

3
00:00:06.366 --> 00:00:08.875
which removes far more
than anyone planned.

4
00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:13.758
Close behind are deleting an app instead of
a grant, and removing a broad permission

5
00:00:13.758 --> 00:00:18.287
before its replacement is in place, which
takes a workload down in production.

6
00:00:18.287 --> 00:00:22.955
Then the subtle ones: a mail scope that
does nothing while the old grant stays,

7
00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:27.918
a narrowing that actually widens, last
quarter's answer passing as this quarter's,

8
00:00:27.918 --> 00:00:31.390
and a permission quietly
re-granted at the next consent.
